    "updated_at": "2022-10-04T09:30:37Z",
    "body": "I don't think there is any major need to synchronize changes, provided changes in DOM and CSP get done before the HTML spec starts referencing the definitions. The event will be defined twice in cross-reference databases until the HTML pull request is merged, but there are no other specs that reference it it any case. Impact on `@webref/events` should be minimal too and we can simply postpone publication of the new version of `@webref/events` until all pull requests are merged.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
